      ],
      "pins": [
        "Q10.3",
        "D5.3",
        "D6.3",
        "D7.3",
        "D18.3",
        "D19.3",
        "D20.3",
        "D21.3"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "Net-(D18-VSS)",
        "GND"
      ],
      "observed": "Q10 is the only low-side path for the VSS pins of all seven WS2812B LEDs, but its metadata specifies a 190 mA NMOS.",
      "expected": "The WS2812B ground switch should be rated for the total LED current; seven WS2812B devices can require well over 190 mA (up to roughly 420 mA at full white).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"Q10\") ... (description \" 60V 190mA 4.5Ω@10V,100mA 2.1V@250uA 1PCSNChannel SOT-23 MOSFETs ROHS\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"119\") (name \"Net-(D18-VSS)\") ... (node (ref \"D5\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"VSS\")) ... (node (ref \"Q10\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"D\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Addressable status LEDs (WS2812B, D5-D7, D18-D21)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the addressable LEDs are driven at moderate to full brightness, Q10 can overheat, current-limit, or fail, causing the LED chain to behave differently or be damaged.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": [
        "U10",
        "U11"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "U10.4",
        "U10.5",
        "U11.4",
        "U11.5"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "GND"
      ],
      "observed": "The isolated CAN transceivers U10 and U11 have both GND1 and GND2 pins connected to the same system GND net.",
      "expected": "For the intended isolated CAN buses, the transceiver secondary ground (GND2) should not be tied directly to the primary/system ground; isolation requires separate ground references.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"80\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\")) (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\")) (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\")) (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (U8, U9) through an isolated CAN transceiver"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The CAN interfaces would not provide the intended galvanic isolation, changing noise/safety behavior from the specified architecture.",
      "confidence": 0.66
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": [
        "D4",
        "D14",
        "D23"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "D4.2",
        "D14.2",
        "D23.2"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW"
      ],
      "observed": "The net /LED_3.3V_POWER_SW contains only the anodes of LEDs D4, D14, and D23, with no power source or driver connected to it.",
      "expected": "An LED anode power net should be connected to a 3.3 V source or a switch/driver that can supply the LEDs; otherwise the LEDs cannot light.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"32\") (name \"/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW\") ... (node (ref \"D14\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\")) (node (ref \"D23\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\")) (node (ref \"D4\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "D4, D14, and D23 will remain dark even when their cathode-side signals are active.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files support at least one real anomaly: the WS2812 ground switch Q10 is undersized for the LED current it carries. The isolated CAN transceiver grounds are also merged with system ground, and a 3.3 V LED power net is left floating, both of which deviate from intended or standard behavior."
}

